# Compiled WASM binaries.
#
# READ THIS BEFORE TRUSTING THE HEADING BELOW. These patterns are ignore rules, not
# statements of fact: six substrate modules ARE tracked (force-added) and are what the
# runner actually loads — dla-canonical-{wat,llvm,emcc,rust,asc,zig}.wasm. Only the Go
# module is genuinely built at run time, because it is ~1.9 MB.
#
# The gap between this file's intent and the tree cost two weeks (2026-08-15):
# `dla-canonical-zig.wasm` was committed as an `ar` archive and nobody re-derived it,
# because everyone read this heading and assumed it was built fresh. If you commit a
# substrate here, `git add -f` it AND record why it is tracked rather than built.
*.wasm
*.wasm.o
*.o
*.a
wasm_exec.js
go.sum

# Build artifacts
zig-cache/
zig-out/
.zig-cache/
